WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.932
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.932 --> 00:00:05.390
SPEAKER: In this
video, we're going

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.240
to walk through how to close
a Cloud billing account using

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.080
the console.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.960
Before closing a
billing account,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.130
remember that you'll need
to be a billing account

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.210
administrator.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.670
Google Cloud Support cannot
close a billing account

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.700
on your behalf.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.690
So reach out to your billing
account admins, if needed.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:23.300
Get started by heading
to the Cloud Console.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.760
You can start on any
project homepage.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.820
Then head to the Navigation
menu in the left-hand pane.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.960
Choose Billing.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.689
And then click Manage
Billing Accounts.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:35.750
Select the name of the billing
account you want to close.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.660
This will open the Billing
Accounts Overview page.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.020
In the left-hand nav,
choose Account Management.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.210
Then click on Close
Billing Account

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.350
located at the top of the page.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.040
The pop-up dialogue contains
important information

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.340
about recommended actions to
take prior to account closing.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.690
Type the word Close and then
click Close Billing Account.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.850
The billing account
is now closed,

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.210
and it's indicated by the red
banner at the top of the page.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.120
Closing the billing account
stops all billable services

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.040
and any projects
linked to the account,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.160
preventing the account from
accruing further charges.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.650
Final charges for the
account will be fully accrued

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.990
48 hours after the
closure and will

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.020
be reflected on your final bill
based on your current billing

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.740
cycle.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.020
This bill will be the
last bill you receive

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.340
unless you reopen the account.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.280
Head over to the documentation
to check out more details.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.630
[MUSIC PLAYING]

